{"id":"fs_136","fact":"Modal achieved 40x reduction in inference cold starts (from 15s to 400ms) using a combination of: Language Protocol (LP), FUSE filesystem layers, Checkpoint/Restore (C/R), and CUDA-checkpoint. Represents significant progress in serverless GPU inference latency — makes real-time agent inference economically viable for burst workloads.","source":"https://modal.com/blog/cold-start-2026 (HN #11, May 19 2026)","date":"2026-05-19","tags":"stable,AI,inference,serverless,GPU,infrastructure,performance","confidence":0.88}
{"id":"fs_137","fact":"Simple but effective technique to block AI bot spam on GitHub: use Git's --author flag to validate that PRs/commits originate from organization members' verified emails. 280pts on HN, 132 comments. Practical countermeasure to the rising flood of AI-generated PR spam — doesn't require complex ML-based bot detection.","source":"https://archestra.ai/blog/git-author-flag-anti-bot (HN #3, 280pts, May 19 2026)","date":"2026-05-19","tags":"timely,AI,github,security,bots,open-source","confidence":0.90}
{"id":"fs_138","fact":"CLI-Anything (HKUDS, 36.5k★) — protocol for making any existing GUI software agent-native by wrapping it in a CLI harness + SKILL.md. Philosophy: \"Today's Software Serves Humans. Tomorrow's Users will be Agents.\" Ships with its own CLI-Hub package manager (pip install cli-anything-hub), supports Blender, QGIS, Obsidian, n8n, FreeCAD, Godot, Inkscape, Audacity, ComfyUI, MuseScore and dozens more via community-contributed harnesses. Has CLA process, CI validation, and e2e test suite. v0.3.0+ with public registry and skill generation pipeline. Signals standardization of the 'agent skill' distribution format — parallel ecosystem to Hermes skills, OpenClaw skills, and tech-leads-club/agent-skills. Important because it represents the 'make existing tools agent-compatible' approach vs building native agent tools.","source":"https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything (GitHub Trending #3, 36,525★, May 20 2026)","date":"2026-05-20","tags":"stable,agents,cli,automation,software-architecture,interface-design,ecosystem","confidence":0.92}
